  "limits": [
    "QA-only fixed scene state and seeded Math.random for repeatable rendering; engine RAF/update/gameplay never started.",
    "natural creates fresh HTMLImage objects; URLs may already be browser cached, including after initial decode warmup. It is not a guaranteed cold-network sample.",
    "fallback explicitly disables all images; ready shares actual decoded requested images. Their different images are diagnostic modes, not optimization A/B or equal-quality alternatives.",
    "Method spans are inclusive and instrumentation has overhead. Existing five render stages are non-overlapping. Readback is artificial and separate. No pure CPU/GPU attribution.",
    "No native gameplay/server/database, strict continuous60s, browser total memory or whole-goal acceptance.",
    "Each measure constructs a fresh Engine and Canvas. Ready means shared decoded images only; ground cache/atlases are cold in that instance. These timings are not warm same-engine walking costs."
  ],
  "next": "Keep startup first use, ready-image first ground draw and warm walking separate. Further evidence must distinguish first vector/text/image submission and scheduling before accepting a candidate; no texture removal or quality reduction.",
